# V3 trade-to-trade monitor

`scripts/aggression_dashboard_v3/` on port `5053` implements `docs/aggression_v1_monitor.tex`. It is not the old V2-copy / flow-effort page.

- Writes only `workspace/analysis/aggression_v3_live/`
- Label `PROVISIONAL / RESEARCH-ONLY / TRADE-TO-TRADE / NON-EXECUTABLE`
- Manual start: `Y:\Aastha\SOD\run_aggression_monitor_v3.bat`
- The parallel session treats `C:\dev\market_data_puller` (branch `ops/local-runtime`) as V3's source of truth and deploys to Y: with `ops\release0\deploy_release0.ps1` (item `v3` = the whole V3 package, its `tests/test_v3_*.py` and the three `aggression_v3_*` research scripts; `v3core` is the older exchange-time subset). Changes made directly on Y: (the 2026-09-25/27 state banners and live chips) must be ported to C:\dev, or a deploy/restore will overwrite them.
- Do not kill/restart 5053 unless the user asks
- Do not edit V1 (5050), V1.3 (5055), or V2 from V3 work
- Offline flow-effort helpers: `scripts/aggression_flow_effort.py`
- Default view is the whole curve (FV+TU+TY+US vs TY price). Live `beta_ref` is today's day-tag beta from `tag_beta.json` (`ensure_beta_ref` → `tag_beta.beta_for_session`). Tags: 2Y/3Y/5Y/7Y/10Y/30Y, AUCTION_OTHER, MONTH_END, TIER1, REGULAR. Fit is the flow-history day OLS; print path reads the file only. The superseded 10-session mean is `ensure_session_mean_beta_ref`.
- Banner READY is gated on live + `beta_ref>0` + window endpoints after the last gap longer than the window. It is not gated on a process-global config key. Peek reads `tag_beta.json`; when the table is behind the last close, one background `v3-beta-ref` thread updates it (V1 `flow_history.sqlite` read-only). Kick only when `stale` / not ok — a stale return must never re-trigger a rebuild (that loop pinned 5053 at 100% CPU for 14 hours). `_kick_beta_ref` calls `offer_history()` only after a fresh OK beta.
- After a code change, the running process keeps the old beta until a **manual** V3 restart (do not kill 5053 unless the user asks).
- Session tape hole-only merge (`print_reconcile.py`), done per rebuild over the whole session by `_live_display_trades` (no separate hist-only store): live first, then hist. Match size / side / tick-price within 1ms; keep stored. Hist fills left/interior holes only; skip interior if match rate < 0.5; never insert hist after the live tail.
- TotalAggress is session-to-date from the first print after 18:00 ET and the Panel 4 path starts at the session's first price (spec). Lookback only clips the charts; never rebuild the sum from the 2-hour window start (that shifted every value, forced a 41 MB `history` resend every rebuild, and left steps at the live tail). `history` only fires when a hole-fill moves a shared value by more than `PREFIX_TOLERANCE`. Prints applied while a rebuild runs (the tail and `kept_rows`) must be re-accumulated onto the rebuilt sum (`_continue_session_sum`, `_continue_kept`); if that moves them past the tolerance, send `history`.
- Backfill `covered_end` is the earliest symbol's last fetched Databento print, never wall-clock `now`; otherwise the next start lands past Databento's ~20-minute availability lag (`422 data_start_after_available_end`) and gaps never fill.
- Page (`static/dashboard.js`): queue trade deltas and redraw charts at most once per second (`LIVE_FLUSH_MS`), min/max-decimate drawn points per pixel bucket, and keep Panel 3 buy/sell as WebGL spikes. Per-message `extendTraces`/`relayout` and SVG bars froze browsers ("page isn't responding") with ~64k prints per 2 hours.
- `_matched_incoming` must stay time-bounded (time-sorted buckets + bisect ±1 ms; ties go to the lowest stored row). A full per-bucket scan is quadratic and took minutes per rebuild on a 2-hour tape.
- `_snapshot_tenday_trades` returns a shared frame (beta refresh only); callers must not modify it in place. Panel 5 (last 10 sessions) was removed 2026-10-23.
- Wire format: the snapshot sends one `prints` column table with `rows: {from, skip}` for Panels 1/3/4 (exactly the old per-panel rows; `panels.print_panel_rows` ↔ `expandPrintColumns`). Hover rows are `compact_banner` (status, state, as_of, window_min, contribution_line, reason, x) and the page expands them from `meta.state_styles`. Live prints carry `h`, never the full `banner`/`hover`. Do not re-add full banners per print or per-panel copies of the print columns.
